course: dictionary
lesson: 11477
title: Showing love in how we act
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Affectionately is an adverb. An adverb tells you how someone does something, and this one often ends in -ly. It means in a loving, caring and gentle way.
explain: «Mum tucked the blanket around me and kissed my forehead affectionately.» The word tells you how she kissed you: with love and gentleness, not in a rush or a cross way. Check it by swapping in lovingly. The sentence still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: Look for clues that show love, such as hugs, smiles, soft voices or a kind nickname. «Our neighbour is affectionately known as "Grandpa Joe", because he always has time for us.» The nickname is given with fondness, so affectionately shows warmth.
fact: Affectionately is an adverb, and it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Affectionately» means in a loving, caring and gentle way.
fact: «Affectionately» often appears in phrases such as «affectionately known as» and «smile affectionately».
fact: A good check is to swap in a word like lovingly or gently and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The old dog nudged the puppy affectionately with his nose.» How did the dog nudge the puppy? | *In a loving, gentle way | Roughly and in a hurry | Angrily, to make it move | Loudly, so everyone could hear
exercise: «Nadia smiled affectionately at her little brother.» Which word is closest in meaning to affectionately? | *Lovingly | Rudely | Angrily | Quickly
exercise: «Ella hugged her cat affectionately.» Which word tells you how Ella hugged? | hugged | cat | *affectionately | Ella
test: «The nurse held the baby affectionately and sang a soft song.» How did the nurse hold the baby? | Sadly | *Gently and with love | Carelessly, as if she was in a hurry | Tightly, to stop it moving
test: Which sentence shows someone acting affectionately? | The bus stopped affectionately | *She patted the puppy affectionately on the head | He slammed the door affectionately | The thunder roared affectionately
exam: Sam says affectionately means angrily. What does it really mean? | In an angry, shouting way | In a sad, quiet way | In a fast, rushing way | *In a loving, caring and gentle way
